From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:37:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] A player's tick makes fewer positions, lists and events
 nobody reads

isWet asks whether it rains before making two positions to ask where;
isInsideOfMaterial, isOnLadder, the friction lookups and a dropped item's read
their block by coordinates; handleFalling makes its position for a landing
only. A sprinting entity's running particle, which the server sends nobody, is
no longer worked out. A move of nothing gathers no collision boxes: a client
standing still sends one every tick. sendPacketNearby asks canSee of the
players in range only. ServerTickStartEvent and ServerTickEndEvent are made for
listeners only, and a world thread walks its worlds by index.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

